+## Three repositories
+
+This repository is the ASSEMBLY ROOT of a three-repository project — the shape
+[openRepoShape](https://github.com/opensoft/openRepoShape) calls the Triad. It
+holds this front door, `project.yaml`, the pins and the gate, and mounts the
+other two as submodules; it holds no product code of its own.
+
+| role | repository | path | holds |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| assembly | `opensoft/openRepoTools` | `.` | the front door, the manifest, the pins, the gate |
+| spec | `opensoft/openRepoTools-spec` | `spec/` | `openspec/`, `specs/`, `docs/` (the manuals), `ideation/` |
+| code | `opensoft/openRepoTools-code` | `code/` | every command below, `repos.tsv`, `skills/`, `commands/`, `tests/`, CI, the pinned standard |
+
+```sh
+git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/opensoft/openRepoTools.git
+cd openRepoTools
+make bootstrap          # each leg on main AT its pinned commit, then the validators
+```
+
+Nothing a person types changes: the commands keep their names and the install
+one-liner below is the same line. A path in this file that begins `spec/` or
+`code/` is relative to this root. `AGENTS-shape.md` is the shape's rules for an
+agent working here, and electing the shape confers nothing.
+
+### The lockstep invariant
+
+For each leg, three things name the same commit and move in ONE commit here:
+the gitlink at the leg's path, `commit:` in `contracts/<role>-pin.yaml`, and
+every `.github/workflows/*.yml` `@<sha>` that names the leg. A change to a leg
+lands in that leg first, by pull request; this root then advances its pin with
+openRepoShape's `scripts/bump-leg.py`, and `make pins` refuses when the three
+disagree.
+
